# Line endings are LF, in the repository and in every checkout.
#
# Without this file git stores whatever the editor happened to write, and this
# repository had drifted to 83 files with LF, 34 with CRLF, and four with both
# inside one file. That is invisible until something rewrites a file wholesale and
# a three-line change arrives as a nine-hundred-line diff, which is exactly the
# review nobody can do.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text, so a binary added later is left alone
# without anyone remembering to say so. `eol=lf` is what makes the working tree
# match, on Windows too -- there is nothing here that needs CRLF: no .bat or .cmd
# files, and the shell scripts are bash.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Vendored third-party files are kept byte-for-byte as published, which is a claim
# their READMEs make and normalisation would quietly break. Nothing under here is ours
# to reformat, and everything under here is checked against an upstream URL.
api/web/vendor/** -text

# Safety net for asset types that would be corrupted if the detection above ever
# guessed wrong. Nothing here yet; vendored fonts and images are the likely arrivals.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
*.zst binary
